  "result": "I found the cause and wrote a plan, but I haven't changed any code. I couldn't call `ExitPlanMode`, so I'm asking for approval here instead.\n\n**Cause:** `Context.__init__` in `src/click/core.py:386-394` hands the subcommand the parent's whole `default_map`. The docs show defaults nested under the subcommand name, such as `{'runserver': {'port': 5000}}`. So the subcommand looks for `port` at the top level, doesn't find it, and ignores the default.\n\n**Fix:** change line 392 to `default_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)`. If the nested value is `UNSET`, treat it as no map.\n\n**Tests:** I'd add a test in `tests/test_defaults.py` for a group with a subcommand. It would check three things:\n- The nested default is applied.\n- A CLI argument overrides it.\n- A missing key falls back to the option's own default.\n\nI'd also add a line to `CHANGES.md`.\n\nApprove and I'll implement it, then run the test suite.",
